<title>USA: Calif. lawmakers debate $350 mln prison bond.</title>
<headline>Calif. lawmakers debate $350 mln prison bond.</headline>
<dateline>SACRAMENTO, Calif. 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>California state lawmakers on Monday will consider a $350 million bond measure to fund construction of prison facilities for young offenders.</p>
<p>A subcommittee of the state Senate's Public Safety panel was expected to vote on Senate Bill 808, the Local Juvenile Justice Facilities Bond Act of 1998, at Monday's hearing.</p>
<p>If approved by state lawmakers, the $350 million general obligation bond measure would be placed on the November 1998 statewide ballot, according to Democratic Senator Jim Costa, who introduced the bond act.</p>
